      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOUISE LUCK (9) was out of the money two runs ago then improved sharply at her latest appearance over 2030m at this track, scoring comfortably by 8 metres after being up on the pace from the outset. Gets a soft run on the inside of the second line but may need luck at some point. This looks a sterner test than last time but she is capable of another big performance. BUBBA NAY (1) failed to flatter last time out when sixth, beaten 18 metres, over 1609m at this track. Form prior to that was strong, including a very close fourth over 2030m at this track two starts ago. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Won't find this any harder and she can finish a lot closer this time. MAYWYNS MIGHTY MAC (8) has been thereabouts of late and is a great chance to break through. Good effort last time out when he finished second at Tamworth over 1609m. MAJOR AUSTIN (7) is in the mix after finishing runner-up for the second time in a row last start, beaten a nose at this track.",
